From: Christopher Owen <3221756+christopherowen@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 01:15:43 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 416/488] [DS4.1] DSpark context-graph inputs in one TileLang
 launch

DSparkContextCudaGraphs.run copied the target's three auxiliary hidden
states into the graph's buffer and scrubbed the tail of the buffer, the
positions and every group's slots: three strided copies and three fills,
eager before each replay. One launch now does both, a block a row and
1024 columns of each source, 16-byte accesses with the three loads
issued before the stores. Declared at model construction; tested bit for
bit against the torch prologue, NaN and infinities included.
